{"game": "risk-of-rain-returns", "language": "english", "appid": 1337520, "month": "2024-02", "window": 2, "start_date": 1707350400, "end_date": 1707955199, "month_true_total": 227, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 00:52:06 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "158337597", "author": {"steamid": "76561198931189316", "personaname": "watersoda", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/watersoda/", "num_games_owned": 73, "num_reviews": 19, "playtime_forever": 1089, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 321, "last_played": 1708134222, "avatar": "313d1028337e8e63122b9181f54fddc82a92b5d3"}, "language": "english", "review": "I have played ror1, and i can say this is a massive step-up in quality; it would deserve the 15$ price, if it weren't for several glaring issues.\n\n1. Enemies are too tanky. Plain and simple.\n\n2. While \"Providence Challenges\" are a cool idea, many have issues regarding difficulty and map design, and seem to default to Monsoon difficulty and cannot be changed. This presents little benefit to newer players, who would otherwise have a less grindy way to unlock skins and skills.\n\n3. Gameplay is still very clunky, despite the new control schemes. Just please let us shoot up.\n\n4 .Enemies are still too tanky,\n\nI'd love for anyone to tell me i'm missing some critical thing, so i can enjoy this game. \nBut for now, i just can't recommend it.\n\n\nEdit: nvm it was just a skill issue", "timestamp_created": 1707953661, "timestamp_updated": 1708062352, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.538412868976593018", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1699469751", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "158335925", "author": {"steamid": "76561198219340444", "personaname": "Wylde", "persona_status": "online", "pro